      "snl": "interface(SnlSyntaxTree,enumerate(Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.macro_name,string),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.style_name,Type.opt(string)),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.env_mode,Type.opt(Type.union(Type.literal(formula_inline),Type.literal(formula_display),Type.literal(text)))),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.kind,string),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.scope,Type.opt(string)),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.mdata,unknown),Type.judge(SnlSyntaxTree.children,Type.array(SnlSyntaxTree))))",
      "markdown": "The principal type for an SNL syntax tree. A node has fields including `macro_name`, `kind`, `children`, `mdata`, `env_mode`, `style_name`, and `scope`. It is a union type combining the three `env_mode` branches: formula, text, and block. All parser output, serializer input, and renderer consumption use this type."
